@startuml Sandbox Environment Setup Sequence

!theme plain
title SABER Docker Sandbox Environment Setup - Current Implementation

actor Agent
participant "SessionManager" as SM
participant "BenchmarkManager" as BM
participant "EpisodeManager" as EM_EP
participant "ExecutionManager" as EM
participant "SandboxEnvironmentManager" as SBMGR
participant "ComposeOrchestrator" as CO
participant "Docker Compose" as DC

== Episode Initialization (Current Flow) ==

Agent -> SM: POST /api/v1/session/{session_id}/episodes?task_id=dvwa_sql_injection
activate SM

SM -> BM: get_task(task_id)
activate BM

BM --> SM: Task (with environment, execution_config, episode_config)
deactivate BM

SM -> SM: create Episode object (state=CREATING)
SM -> EM_EP: add_episode_to_session(session_id, episode)
activate EM_EP
EM_EP --> SM: episode tracked
deactivate EM_EP

SM -> SM: session.add_creating_episode(episode_id)
SM -> SM: handle dependency resolution if needed (with retry)

== Task Configuration and Environment Setup ==

SM -> EM: configure_for_task(episode_id, task, session_id, target_episode_id)
activate EM

note over EM
ExecutionManager configures from task object:
- Initializes SandboxEnvironmentManager if needed
- Creates episode-specific environment immediately
- Configures ExecutorFactory with task config
- Handles network attachment for dependent episodes
end note

EM -> SBMGR: create_episode_environment_async(episode_id, task.environment, target_episode_id, session_id)
activate SBMGR

SBMGR -> CO: new ComposeOrchestrator(logging_config)
activate CO

CO -> CO: resolve compose file path from task.environment
CO -> DC: docker-compose up -d (NO health checks)
activate DC

DC -> DC: Start containers without waiting for health
DC --> CO: Containers starting
deactivate DC

CO --> SBMGR: (orchestrator, compose_path)
deactivate CO

SBMGR --> EM: Environment started (health checks pending)
deactivate SBMGR

EM -> EM: reset executor factory for new sandbox manager
EM --> SM: configure_for_task_async complete
deactivate EM

SM -> SM: session.move_to_active_episode(episode_id)
SM -> SM: Release episode creation lock

== Background Finalization (runs concurrently) ==

SM -> SM: spawn _finalize_episode_creation background task
note over SM
Background finalization:
1. Wait for health checks (with semaphore limit)
2. Generate prompts via PromptGenerator
3. policy_manager.set_episode_policy(episode_id, session_id, prompt)
4. episode_manager.configure_for_task(episode_id, task)
5. Copy initial files to execution container
6. Configure evaluation manager
7. mark_episode_ready(episode_id)
end note

SM --> Agent: EpisodeCreateResponse{episode_id, state=CREATING}
deactivate SM

== Client Polls for Episode Status ==

Agent -> SM: GET /api/v1/session/{session_id}/episodes/{episode_id}/status
SM --> Agent: EpisodeStatusResponse{state=READY} (after finalization completes)

== Command Execution with Episode Context ==

Agent -> SM: MCP tool call: cli(command="nmap dvwa_webapp") with headers
note right of Agent
Headers include:
- X-SABER-Session-ID: {session_id}
- X-SABER-Episode-ID: {episode_id}
- X-SABER-Orchestration-Env: {orchestration_env}
end note
activate SM

SM -> SM: validate episode is active in session
SM -> EM: step(action, context) with episode context
activate EM

EM -> EM: get_executor(action.tool_name, episode_id)
EM -> EM: validate_parameters(action.parameters)
EM -> SBMGR: get_episode_environment(episode_id)
activate SBMGR

note over SBMGR
Environment was created during episode initialization,
so it already exists and is ready for command execution
end note

SBMGR --> EM: ComposeOrchestrator for episode
deactivate SBMGR

EM -> CO: execute command in episode-specific containers
activate CO

note over CO
Command executes in episode-specific execution container
with access to episode-specific target services
via Docker Compose internal networking
end note

CO -> CO: run command via docker exec
CO --> EM: CommandResult(success=True, data="Host dvwa_webapp is up...")
deactivate CO

EM --> SM: CommandResult
deactivate EM

SM -> EM_EP: step(episode_id, action, command_result)
activate EM_EP
EM_EP -> EM_EP: create and add step to episode
EM_EP --> SM: StepResult(step, should_terminate=False)
deactivate EM_EP

SM --> Agent: MCP result with nmap output
deactivate SM

== Episode Cleanup ==

Agent -> SM: DELETE /api/v1/session/{session_id}/episodes/{episode_id}
activate SM

SM -> EM_EP: end_episode(episode_id, reason, result)
activate EM_EP
EM_EP -> EM_EP: update episode state and completion info
EM_EP --> SM: Episode completed
deactivate EM_EP

SM -> EM: cleanup_episode(episode_id)
activate EM

EM -> SBMGR: stop_episode_environment(episode_id)
activate SBMGR

SBMGR -> CO: stop_environment(compose_file_path, episode_id)
activate CO

CO -> DC: docker-compose down --volumes
activate DC

DC -> DC: Stop and remove episode containers, networks, volumes
DC --> CO: Episode environment cleaned up
deactivate DC

CO --> SBMGR: Episode cleanup complete
deactivate CO

SBMGR --> EM: Episode environment removed
deactivate SBMGR

EM --> SM: Episode cleanup complete
deactivate EM

SM -> SM: _cleanup_episode_network_with_retry(episode_id)

== Session Cleanup ==

Agent -> SM: DELETE /api/v1/session/{session_id}
activate SM

SM -> EM: cleanup_session_environments(session_id)
activate EM
EM -> SBMGR: cleanup all remaining episode environments
EM --> SM: All environments cleaned
deactivate EM

SM --> Agent: 200 OK - Session terminated
deactivate SM

note over Agent, DC
**Current Sandbox Environment Implementation**

**Key Architecture Principles:**
- Async environment creation: Docker compose starts immediately, health checks run in background
- Episode state lifecycle: CREATING -> READY -> ACTIVE -> COMPLETED
- Global episode creation lock serializes Docker Compose operations
- Background finalization with semaphore-limited concurrent health checks
- Episode-based environment isolation with unique container naming
- Episode dependency resolution with retry logic for race conditions

**Environment Management:**
- task.environment specifies static compose file template name
- SandboxEnvironmentManager.create_episode_environment_async() starts containers without blocking
- ComposeOrchestrator handles Docker Compose operations directly
- Episode-specific environment variables (EPISODE_ID, SESSION_ID) for container naming
- Optional network attachment for dependent episodes via target_episode_id

**Execution Flow:**
1. Episode creation acquires global lock for Docker serialization
2. Episode created in CREATING state, added to creating_episode_ids
3. ExecutionManager.configure_for_task_async() starts containers (no health checks)
4. Episode moves to active_episode_ids, lock released
5. Background task runs health checks, prompts, file copies, marks READY
6. Client polls status until episode is READY
7. MCP commands execute with episode context via headers
8. Episode cleanup removes all episode-specific resources + networks

**Current Implementation Details:**
- REST API: POST /api/v1/session/{session_id}/episodes?task_id=...
- Response returns immediately with state=CREATING
- MCP headers required: X-SABER-Session-ID, X-SABER-Episode-ID, X-SABER-Orchestration-Env
- Episode-based concurrency limits (max 3 concurrent per episode)
- Fail-fast parameter validation and error handling
- Complete environment isolation per episode
- Client-side benchmark orchestration and evaluation
- Network cleanup with retry logic to prevent subnet pool exhaustion
end note

@enduml
